<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch April consumer prices rise 1.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch April consumer prices rise 1.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch consumer price index (CPI) was provisionally unchanged in April against March, giving a 1.8 percent year-on-year rise, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH CONSUMER PRICE INFLATION   April 97   March 97   April 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI pct change		unch	  0.6	  0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	  1.8	  2.0	  2.0</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		    118.9	118.9	116.8</p>
<p>NOTES - Economists had expected the April CPI to rise between 1.8 percent and 2.2 percent year-on-year (consensus 2.0)  </p>
<p>EU-HARMONISED DUTCH INFLATION</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	  1.2	  1.3	  1.4</p>
<p> Index (base 1996)		    101.7	101.6	100.5</p>
<p>The detailed non-harmonised index figures were:</p>
<p>					    Weighting   April 97  March 97</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco			 180     110.4     110.3</p>
<p> Clothes, shoes				  72     101.7     101.5</p>
<p> Rent, heating, lighting		    261     132.5     132.5</p>
<p> Furniture, household appliances etc.    80     106.9     106.9</p>
<p> Medical care				     6     120.5     119.8</p>
<p> Transport, communication		   144     119.5     119.6</p>
<p> Leisure, education			   107     108.5     108.8</p>
<p> Other goods, services			113     117.7     117.4</p>
<p> Consumer taxes, govt. services	    37     154.7     154.7</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 570 8500</p>
</text>
